# CPU-write checks by block (27 Nov): every draw asked the memory tracker for the ranges the CPU wrote (taking its
# lock), and every non-empty answer walked all the guest textures kept (thousands: ~5 minutes of them) to mark the
# ones on those ranges. Explosions write guest memory between most draws, so that walk ran hundreds of times a frame
# inside the "setup" phase. Textures are now listed by the 64 KB blocks of their ranges and a write checks only the
# textures on its blocks; the tracker skips its lock when nothing is queued. BOTS_GFX_TEXTURE_INDEX=0: the full walk
# (A/B). With BOTS_DRAW_PROFILE=1 a line per stats window, "CPU-write checks per frame": batches, ranges, time,
# textures checked and marked changed.
